Package: RoCE
Type: Package
Title: RoCE: Robust Federated Causal Estimation through Calibrated High-Dimensional Models
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-08-25
Authors@R: 
    person("Sinian", "Zhang", 
           email = "zhan9381@umn.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Sinian Zhang [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Sinian Zhang <zhan9381@umn.edu>
Description: Implements federated learning algorithms for causal inference in 
    multi-site settings. The primary estimator targets the target average
    treatment effect (TATE) by fitting arm-specific nuisance functions and
    directly aggregating treated-minus-control source-assisted estimators with
    a common source-weight vector. Arm-specific potential-outcome means
    mu^a_t = E_t[Y(a)] remain available for diagnostics and secondary analyses.
    The package provides two-round and one-round communication protocols with
    two-level cross-fitting for enhanced robustness against overfitting bias.
    It includes doubly robust estimators with calibrated loss functions,
    variance-minimizing source aggregation, binomial and Gaussian generalized
    linear models, C++-accelerated coordinate descent and cross-validation,
    and target-only, sample-size weighted, inverse-variance weighted, and
    doubly robust comparison estimators.
